mend is  a d3 if NC tank built for a variation of  this this build excels at being up close  and even with the team that has no idea  what they're doing you'll comfortably be  able to carry them through you'll be  able to mow down close range NPCs  gaining a massive amount of health on  kill and even if the NPC's are at range  you have the shield to protect you  they're running with the team or with  randoms I recommend running the d5 is  your second skill because you'll also  end up being the team Reviver when  things go wrong in the previous assault  global event I actually found it easier  and faster  solo through the missions because the  enemies were even weaker and fewer and  number and would match made groups I  found I was spending more time keeping  allies alive than shooting at the NPC's  in turn making the build less effective  a couple of the masks in this event  required a run with a team as you can  see here I didn't manage to collect them  all last time remember to make sure that  all of the conditions have been set up  properly in order to obtain the masks  the first mask  haki is fairly easy to obtain kill 500  LMB and the assault playlist with the  crucial or major modifier activated you  don't really have to hunt this one down  just play the game as usual and you'll  eventually get this the second mask  happy requires you to complete each  assault playlist mission without agent  or agents being downed most of these  missions can be so load but the Falcon  lost incursion can be tricky on your own  so in order to unlock this known and the  team can be downed personally I'll be  attempting to solo this but if you were  to get a group together let the others  know what you're trying to achieve the  third mask and assault is picky although  this must be running groups this is  actually a little bit easier than masks  to being downed or wiping will not fail  the commendation you just have to make  sure that no one in the group is running  mythical skills it'll take a bit longer  than usual to complete the incursion but  there are checkpoints every few waves so  just take your time and make your way  through them  the third global event is strike this is  all about stacker and explosions but  mainly Steger get too close to a down to  MPC the explosion will stagger you take  too many hits you will explode and  stagger get too close to an ally when  they explode from damage and your  stagger this is probably the least fun  global event to play out of the four but  working through it will give you the  opportunity to collect two of the best  solo player classified sets in the game  nomads and d3 fnc and also the much  loved and loathed pvp set predators mark  the global modifier has NPCs exploding  after being killed so try and avoid  getting too close the pre-emptive and  tactical modifiers will have agents who  sustain too much damage triggering off  an explosion - and have to close to  another agent they will receive  increased damage from the explosion it  is possible to create chain reactions  among the NPC explosions but the most  memorable thing about this event is the  stagger because your allies are  exploding left right and center as best  to keep distance from them if anything  just to decrease the amount of stagger  time you'll be facing the two builds  around most during this event was nomads  and d3 if NC the main reason being that  the amount of explosions going on does  have an impact on your health over time  so you want a builder can really look  after itself again I would probably  favor the d3 build as a solo player  because the shield can stop a lot of the  damage you're taking minimizing yourself  explosions but try not to get too close  if you're good with using cover and  would like a bit more range go for the  Nomad build on the positive side the  masks in this event are really easy to  obtain they can all be gathered running  Solo masks one rider is awarded to you  when you complete any strike activity  without taking any explosion damage the  best way to do this is to sit back with  a range to a skill power build and  slowly make your way through the mission  if you take any damage fall back until  your damage bar drops down mask to  classic requires you to run through a  mission in a group and not take any  explosion damage from an ally you can  easily choose this commendation by  running through the mission solo it  doesn't matter if you take explosion  damage from yourself so just fight your  way through to the end  killing all enemies apart from the boss  once you're there put yourself somewhere  safe and start matchmaking as soon as  someone joins you finish off the boss  both you and the joining agent will  receive a commendation and the mask mask  three jungle it's a little bit more  grindy you'll need patience for this one  you need to kill a total of 150 Ryker  bosses these can be obtained from  anywhere dark zone light zone bosses and  missions but if you're willing to sit  back and grind for it the fastest way is  to equip yourself with a full firearms  build and a bolt-action sniper change  over the world Tier one and run through  to the end of Lexington event center  when you get to the final boss room  you'll see lhara garret and two heavies  standing on stage if you can one-shot  Lara before they're alerted to your  presence this will count as a Ryker boss  skill you can then that the heavies kill  you and rinse and repeat please note if  you don't manage to kill her in one shot  or you miss let the heavies kill you and  try again  this is boring and will probably take  you about an hour to complete so just do  a few at a time or maybe leave it until  the end of the event when you may have  already acquired a few boss kills global  event 4 is ambush the idea here is to  not move the global modifier is agents  deal increased damage while stationary  this sounds a little boring but with the  right build it can actually be a lot of  fun the cover and strategic modifiers  further add to this by damage over time  when moving and even more damage over  time when close to allies this isn't as  difficult as it sounds when you think of  increased damage while not moving two  builds come to mind a sniper built or  better yet a damage dealing skill power  build tactician x' your seeker minds and  bfb sticky bombs are in their element  here using this all of the content is  easy the damage you can get out of  skills during this event is massive I  was never a huge fan of sticky bombs  before this event now I'll always have a  built safe to my loadout  this event has some of the coolest  looking masks much like strike these are  quite easy to achieve mask 1 cage kill  400 enemies while stationary you won't  have to do anything different for this  one just run through this event normally  and you'll have acquired and no time  masks to bug kill 100 enemies whilst  moving again quite easy you may want to  switch up builds to something that can  take a bit more damage but just make  sure you're moving mask 3 haze kill 250  enemies whilst near an ally and  strategic ambush you'll find this easier  with a friend using a healer built to  counter the added damage but even in  matchmaking it's perfectly achievable  you may just find a few people get upset  with you for the extra damage they're  receiving I would have loved to cover  more of the combinations and how you can  complete them but due to the very small  amount of time in between each global  event this month I wanted to get this  out before GE 2 started as I said  earlier the recommendations here are  based on beginner builds to give players  new to these events a good place to  start so if you have more in the way of  gear you can still take the same  principles here and apply them to your  own build if there are further questions  on the global events that I might be  able to quickly answer let me know in  the comments below otherwise thanks for  watching a